I was actually able to bring back Unifi 9:

pkg update -f
pkg install -y -U os-unifi9-maxit
service unifi start
Installed versions:

 os-unifi9-maxit-1.4
 unifi9-9.5.21_3
 mongodb70-7.0.37
 openjdk17-17.0.18+8.1
And running version:

# curl -sk https://10.0.0.1:8443/status
{"meta":{"rc":"ok","up":true,"server_version":"9.5.21","uuid":"5236bf6c-21c1-4701-8f1b-a6f07f8a1d35"},"data":[]}
Once it was all up and running again, I upgraded to Unifi 10 by switching packages:

service unifi stop
pkg delete -y os-unifi9-maxit unifi9
pkg install -n -U os-unifi-maxit  # dry run
pkg install -y -U os-unifi-maxit
service unifi start
All up and running now.
